China's most valuable tech companies, the ripples extend far beyond ByteDance's stock price. Here's why the international tech community should pay attention:"}]]}],["$","p","24",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","strong","0",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"1. China's AI Leadership is Fragile"}]]}],["$","p","25",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"ByteDance was positioned as China's answer to OpenAI. Its Seed team, launched with massive fanfare and funding, was developing foundational models including Doubao—the AI assistant that's become the most popular consumer AI app in China. If ByteDance can't retain talent, what does this mean for China's broader AI competitiveness?"}]]}],["$","p","27",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","strong","0",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"2. Tencent's Strategic Coup"}]]}],["$","p","28",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"With 30+ former Seed engineers now at Tencent, the WeChat parent is quietly assembling one of China's most formidable AI research teams. This represents a fundamental shift in China's AI power dynamics."}]]}],["$","p","30",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","strong","0",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"3. The OpenAI Effect"}]]}],["$","p","31",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Many departing engineers cited working conditions and research freedom as key reasons for leaving. Chinese AI labs are discovering that throwing money at researchers isn't enough—culture and autonomy matter."}]]}],["$","hr","33",{"style":{"border":"none","borderTop":"1px solid #1a1a1a","margin":"32px 0"}}],["$","h2","35",{"style":{"fontSize":"28px","fontWeight":"600","margin":"40px 0 20px","color":"#f5f5f5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"The Exodus: A Timeline of Departures"}]]}],["$","p","37",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"The Seed team's talent drain didn't happen overnight. It's the culmination of a year-long bleed that accelerated dramatically in late 2025."}]]}],["$","div","46",{"style":{"overflowX":"auto","margin":"24px 0"},"children":["$","table",null,{"style":{"width":"100%","borderCollapse":"collapse","fontSize":"14px"},"children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","th","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Quarter"}]]}],["$","th","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Estimated Departures"}]]}],["$","th","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Notable Moves"}]]}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","0",{"children":[["$","td","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Q2 2025"}]]}],["$","td","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"8-10"}]]}],["$","td","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Early departures to startups"}]]}]]}],["$","tr","1",{"children":[["$","td","0",