nce exodus is the Chinese equivalent of the Google Brain → OpenAI migration of 2015. When top talent votes with their feet, it signals something fundamental about the organization's trajectory.\"*"}]]}],["$","p","1",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"— @TechHistorian_Prof · Twitter/X · ❤️ 3.4k"}]]}]]}],["$","blockquote","360",{"style":{"borderLeft":"4px solid #22d3ee","paddingLeft":"24px","margin":"24px 0","fontStyle":"italic","color":"#a3a3a3"},"children":[["$","p","0",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"\"What's fascinating is that Chinese AI talent is no longer choosing between domestic Big Tech and US labs. The startup ecosystem—Moonshot, MiniMax, StepFun—offers a third path that's increasingly attractive.\""}]]}]]}],["$","p","360",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":">"}]]}],["$","blockquote","363",{"style":{"borderLeft":"4px solid #22d3ee","paddingLeft":"24px","margin":"24px 0","fontStyle":"italic","color":"#a3a3a3"},"children":[["$","p","0",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"*\"What's fascinating is that Chinese AI talent is no longer choosing between domestic Big Tech and US labs. The startup ecosystem offers a third path that's increasingly attractive.\"*"}]]}],["$","p","1",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"— @VC_Analyst_Asia · LinkedIn · ❤️ 1.8k"}]]}]]}],["$","hr","364",{"style":{"border":"none","borderTop":"1px solid #1a1a1a","margin":"32px 0"}}],["$","h2","366",{"style":{"fontSize":"28px","fontWeight":"600","margin":"40px 0 20px","color":"#f5f5f5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"What's Next for ByteDance?"}]]}],["$","p","368",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"The question on everyone's mind: Can ByteDance recover from this brain drain?"}]]}],["$","p","370",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","strong","0",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"Short-term (6-12 months):"}],["$","span","1",{"children":" Expect continued attrition as remaining engineers with transferable skills exercise their options. ByteDance will likely accelerate external hiring, but finding 70 qualified AI researchers in this market will take 18-24 months."}]]}],["$","p","372",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","strong","0",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"Medium-term (1-2 years):"}],["$","span","1",{"children":" Seed's research output will likely decline. Projects will be delayed, and Doubao's competitive position may weaken as rivals catch up. ByteDance may be forced to pivot from pure research to acquisition-based AI capabilities."}]]}],["$","p","374",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","strong","0",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"Long-term (3+ years):"}],["$","span","1",{"children":" If the talent exodus isn't reversed, ByteDance risks becoming a follower rather than a leader in AI. The company may retreat to its strength—content recommendation algorithms—while ceding generative AI leadership to Tencent and Alibaba."}]]}],["$","h3","376",{"style":{"fontSize":"22px","fontWeight":"600","margin":"32px 0 16px","color":"#f5f5f5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Strategic Options"}]]}],["$","div","385",{"style":{"overflowX":"auto","margin":"24px 0"},"children":["$","table",null,{"style":{"width":"100%","borderCollapse":"collapse","fontSize":"14px"},"children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","th","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"c