"lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"For ByteDance specifically, the road ahead is uncertain. The company still possesses enormous resources, vast data, and a global user base. But without the talent to translate those advantages into AI breakthroughs, it risks becoming the IBM of the generative AI era—a company with history and scale, but not the cutting edge."}]]}],["$","p","398",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"The question now is whether ByteDance can learn from this crisis, or if the exodus will continue until Seed is merely a shell of its former ambitions. The next 12 months will tell us everything."}]]}],["$","hr","400",{"style":{"border":"none","borderTop":"1px solid #1a1a1a","margin":"32px 0"}}],["$","p","402",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"*Disclaimer: This article is based on publicly available information, media reports, and industry analysis. Specific employee counts and compensation figures are estimates based on multiple sources. ByteDance has not officially confirmed the exact number of departures.*"}]]}],["$","p","404",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","strong","0",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"Reading Time:"}],["$","span","1",{"children":" 18 minutes  "}]]}],["$","p","405",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","strong","0",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"Published:"}],["$","span","1",{"children":" April 14, 2026"}]]}],["$","hr","407",{"style":{"border":"none","borderTop":"1px solid #1a1a1a","margin":"32px 0"}}],["$","p","409",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["